{
  "uid": "slowloris-lab",
  "title": "Slowloris / DDoS Lab",
  "description": "Live view of a Slowloris attack against a deliberately under-provisioned Apache prefork server.",
  "tags": ["lab", "ddos", "slowloris"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "refresh": "2s",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "time": { "from": "now-15m", "to": "now" },
  "templating": { "list": [] },
  "annotations": { "list": [] },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Website reachable",
      "description": "blackbox_exporter probing http://<victim>/ from the observer. 1 = HTTP 200, 0 = timeout or error.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "probe_success{job=\"blackbox\"}",
          "legendFormat": "probe"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "red", "value": null },
              { "color": "green", "value": 1 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Busy Apache workers",
      "description": "apache_workers{state=\"busy\"}. The server has exactly 40 of these.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 6, "y": 0 },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "apache_workers{state=\"busy\", role=\"victim\"}",
          "legendFormat": "busy"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "max": 40,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "#EAB839", "value": 24 },
              { "color": "red", "value": 38 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Peak in-flight connections",
      "description": "Highest single scoreboard bucket: how many connections Apache is juggling right now.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 12, "y": 0 },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "max(apache_scoreboard{role=\"victim\"})",
          "legendFormat": "connections"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "green", "value": null },
              { "color": "#EAB839", "value": 24 },
              { "color": "red", "value": 38 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Availability (last 5 min)",
      "description": "Percentage of blackbox probes that succeeded over the trailing 5 minutes.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 6, "x": 18, "y": 0 },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "avg_over_time(probe_success{job=\"blackbox\"}[5m]) * 100",
          "legendFormat": "availability"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "decimals": 1,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              { "color": "red", "value": null },
              { "color": "#EAB839", "value": 95 },
              { "color": "green", "value": 99.5 }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Website response time (blackbox probe)",
      "description": "End-to-end time to fetch the homepage, measured from a completely separate host.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 6 },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "probe_duration_seconds{job=\"blackbox\"}",
          "legendFormat": "response time"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true, "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineWidth": 2, "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Apache worker slots: busy vs idle",
      "description": "The clearest single picture of the attack: idle collapses to zero and busy pins at 40.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 6 },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "apache_workers{role=\"victim\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{state}}"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true, "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineWidth": 2, "fillOpacity": 12, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "busy" },
            "properties": [{ "id": "color", "value": { "mode": "fixed", "fixedColor": "red" } }]
          },
          {
            "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "idle" },
            "properties": [{ "id": "color", "value": { "mode": "fixed", "fixedColor": "green" } }]
          }
        ]
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Apache connections by state (mod_status scoreboard)",
      "description": "THE slowloris signature. 'read' means 'connected, waiting for request headers' -- exactly where a Slowloris socket parks itself. 'keepalive' is idle keep-alive slots.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 16 },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "sum by (state) (apache_scoreboard{role=\"victim\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{state}}"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "right", "showLegend": true, "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 55,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": { "mode": "normal" }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Established TCP connections on the victim",
      "description": "Kernel-level view from node_exporter. Compare with the scoreboard panel -- the difference is sockets sitting in the accept queue.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 16 },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "node_netstat_Tcp_CurrEstab{role=\"victim\"}",
          "legendFormat": "established"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "node_sockstat_TCP_inuse{role=\"victim\"}",
          "legendFormat": "sockets in use"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true, "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineWidth": 2, "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Attack volume: established connections held by the attackers",
      "description": "Summed across all three attacker nodes. This is the 'distributed' half of the DDoS.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 26 },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "sum(node_netstat_Tcp_CurrEstab{role=\"attacker\"})",
          "legendFormat": "all attackers"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "node_netstat_Tcp_CurrEstab{role=\"attacker\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{node_name}}"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true, "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineWidth": 2, "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Victim CPU and memory headroom",
      "description": "Slowloris is not a CPU attack: CPU barely moves while the site is dead. Memory drops because each prefork worker costs RSS.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 26 },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "100 * (1 - avg(rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode=\"idle\", role=\"victim\"}[1m])))",
          "legendFormat": "CPU used %"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "100 * node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes{role=\"victim\"} / node_memory_MemTotal_bytes{role=\"victim\"}",
          "legendFormat": "memory available %"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true, "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "min"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineWidth": 2, "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Victim network throughput",
      "description": "The point of Slowloris: this stays in the tens of kilobytes per second while the site is unavailable.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 36 },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "sum(rate(node_network_receive_bytes_total{role=\"victim\", device!~\"lo|veth.*|docker.*\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "received"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "sum(rate(node_network_transmit_bytes_total{role=\"victim\", device!~\"lo|veth.*|docker.*\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "transmitted"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true, "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps",
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineWidth": 2, "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "TCP socket states on the victim",
      "description": "TIME_WAIT climbs after the attack stops; sockets in use tracks the attack while it runs.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 36 },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "node_sockstat_TCP_inuse{role=\"victim\"}",
          "legendFormat": "in use"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "node_sockstat_TCP_tw{role=\"victim\"}",
          "legendFormat": "time wait"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus" },
          "expr": "node_sockstat_TCP_alloc{role=\"victim\"}",
          "legendFormat": "allocated"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true, "calcs": ["lastNotNull", "max"] },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineWidth": 2, "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },

    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Running the demo",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 46 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Running the demo\n\n1. **Before the attack** — open the victim site in a second tab and let the client-side probe settle. Point at the *Apache worker slots* panel: 40 workers, most of them idle.\n2. **Start it** — `./scripts/attack.sh start` (SSHes to all three attackers and starts `lab-slowloris`).\n3. **Watch** — within a few seconds `idle` goes to 0, `busy` pins at 40, and the `read` bucket in the scoreboard panel explodes. The blackbox probe turns red and availability drops off a cliff.\n4. **Show the network panel** — throughput stays tiny. This is not a bandwidth attack; a bigger pipe would not help.\n5. **Stop it** — `./scripts/attack.sh stop`. Recovery takes a moment because half-open sockets have to time out.\n6. **The fix** — see the *Hardening* section of the repo README: re-enable `mod_reqtimeout`, or put a buffer in front that only forwards complete headers.\n"
      }
    }
  ]
}
